# Wave T45 (Heritage kit): flowerurn — a stone urn spilling flowers, seated at the avenue's head (12,5) and the statue garden's east gate (8,14) beside the statue keeper's post — the travellers'-flowers dressing of the town tale carried to the town's gates. Weathered stone, a green spill, blossom flecks in pink, cream and gold. Fully opaque: the town grass is baked in (measured #0e7f08). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T45-HERITAGE-PLAN.md §5.)
